Z||000007||grinthock||07-12-2001||03:30 PM||||Oh so is that how it works, unless I spend $15K all at once on a friggen 3.8sc swap job then I don't get the time of day???<P>Let's figure it all out<P>$2800 -- Engine Job<BR>$5000 -- 87GT<BR>$2600 -- Engine Job<P>And I have various other THOUSANDS that I spent on brakes, suspension and the like, If I ain't a good custom, **** !<P>And the excuse they are busy isn't good enough, I have been there and watched the phoen ring off the hook and they don't answer, and I have sent emails and they do'nt answer, OR I get a call 3-4 DAYS later.<P>"Grinthock, simmer down man. They've been at Darknights all week-end. The shop has been closed."<P>Jay -- It's an ongoing issue of degraded service over the past year...  <P>As for the shop being redone -- I heard, can't wait to see it.....  But considering I heard you can't look at your own car on the hoist anymore I may start going elsewhere, the one thing that was nice is they were easy going about letting you poke at your car while it was up (assuming you were out of the way).... Most of the reason for that restriction comes around insurance, and the fact that some idiots start touching OTHER stuff in the shop<P>Don't get me wrong everyone they do GREAT work and I have never had a problem, just contacting them is a REAL B1TCH!<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mach10||07-12-2001||04:20 PM||||I'm going to agree with Grinthock, here. Part of running a successful business is being available for your customers. Whether I need a $2.00 set of fastners, or doing a $500K Ferrari V-12 swap, I should be recieving the same standard of service. Nothing iritates me more than a place putting me on hold, ignoring messages etc., when I'm not spending a huge chunk, then being best buddies when I start talking expensive. Consistency is key. <BR>However, if Fieroshop is going through some localized difficulties etc., then THEY should be advertizing the fact, and offering apologies, not another customer. Please note, though, that they shouldn't HAVE to do it via Forum, unless they use this as an avenue of business as well.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000009||Jay||07-12-2001||06:06 PM||||The point is that they don't use this forum or even look at it, so why say things that they can't defend?  The shop is a mess, they are renovating and the office is now in the back.  As far as being able to watch your car being worked on, yeah it was nice to do that, but, Joe could never get anything done.  Everyone comes by to shoot the $hit and before you know it you've wasted the whole day and nothing is done.  I've been guilty of  that myself and I don't blame them.  Yes it is insurance regulations but it is also a matter of wasted time chating and screwing the pooch.  Everytime I've called they've answered.  Justin, knowing the way you are I would avoid you like the plague as well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  If you want to watch your car being worked on, then do it yourself.  Ferrari dosn't let you hang around while they work on your Italian supercar, why should Joe?||||reg||1
Z||000010||grinthock||07-12-2001||06:16 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>The point is that they don't use this forum or even look at it, so why say things that they can't defend?  ?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>One of their employees reads it on a daily basis and reports back, I know that for a fact.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>The shop is a mess, they are renovating and the office is now in the back.  As far as being able to watch your car being worked on, yeah it was nice to do that, but, Joe could never get anything done.  Everyone comes by to shoot the $hit and before you know it you've wasted the whole day and nothing is done.  <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep. I know, I watch these losers come in while he's working on my car and slow him down that's why it takes so long to get stuff done, I usually ask the "boss" to leave a msg for him and I get back to him (if possible)<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>I've been guilty of  that myself and I don't blame them. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Also Guilty -- But I am better, I only do it if it's URGENT, and short otherwise I arrange a time to talk on the phone or otherwise... and even then it's short, he can't be doing advice all day for free.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR> Yes it is insurance regulations but it is also a matter of wasted time chating and screwing the pooch.  Everytime I've called they've answered.  Justin, knowing the way you are I would avoid you like the plague as well    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>HEY!  Gimmie a break, I wo'nt get into the issues I had Jason....  Just drop that one.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR> If you want to watch your car being worked on, then do it yourself.  Ferrari dosn't let you hang around while they work on your Italian supercar, why should Joe?[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have to agree, they do have a window, so you can look, I was just stating it was NICE before.  What bugs me the most is how certain customs that I know get SUPER gold star treatment, I know guys who call and get appointments NEXT DAY and when I call the same day it's a week.  <P><BR>As much as I do'nt want to take my car elsewhere I might have to now.  <P>And after this post I do'nt expect any favors or otherwise from them now... Even though all I am doing is speaking my mind and truth.<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
