Z||000014||grinthock||07-17-2001||07:35 PM||||I hate to bump old topics to the top, but I think I need to clarify some issues....<P><BR>I do'nt have a problem with the FieroShop... Excluding that I leave messages and don't get calls back too often... This remains a fact, but I think I came down a little hard on them.<P>I need everyone to know that I ABSOLUTLY reccommend their work, but I also reccommend that you call early when you need them, as they are VERY busy, people from all over North AMERICA come there for work, I always see New York, Ohio and others in there getting work done.<P>Their work is 2nd to none when it comes to the Fiero and their shop rates are AMAZING (I do'nt recall what it is, geez, JAY help me out here) and their parts prices are resonable, they also engineer some great products for the Fiero Family of cars.<P>The problems I have experiences should be gone by now however, consider<P>1)  MAJOR shop construction<BR>2)  They lost one of their employees<BR>3)  Increased Business<BR>4)  This is also race season<P><BR>These factors probably caused the slight amount of bad service that I received.  As for bengal's comment that sent me off the deep end, YEP that was out of line, but what can I say, through some FUEL at a fire and it flares up (I was wrong!)<P>Since then,<P>1)  They have hired another Mech, someone who I know from his previous experience and is VERY good!<P>2)  Shop construction has completed<P>I would hope they have not lost customers or lost potential customer because of my comments.  <P>Please accept my sincere apology guys.  ||||reg||4
Z||000015||BENGAL4||07-18-2001||10:24 AM||||Grinthock,<P>Since you stated that my comment was out of line, let me educate you about the business world.<P>I sell tools & construction supplies for a living. In a perfect world, the customer whos spends $10.00, should be treated the same as one who spends thousands of dollars. I try to do this with my customers, but when a big account calls, you jump through hoops to take care of them. It might not be fair, but that is how it is.<P>Race-Tech had my car for well over a year. They did a great job and I am satisfied, but I was also frustrated because it took so long. I picked it up on July 4 and when I was 150 miles from home, in the middle of nowhere, the A/C compressor locked up and it threw a belt. After I get the car home, I have to call Joe to get the bugs out. After 3 or 4 calls and faxes, the problem is solved and the car is running great. I know the shop is very busy and that is why I was so patient waiting for my car. <P>I want to praise Joe for the work he did on my conversion. The car screams. A freind of mine, said riding in it was like going to the amusement park.<P>Grinthock, now that you know the whole story, maybe you realize where I was coming from with my statement. They just wanted to get my car running and me happy.<P>Bill<BR>86GT 3800 Series II S/C<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Slammed Fiero||07-18-2001||10:59 AM||||Bill:<P>Lets get to the important facts.<P>What tranny are you running , does the car have a dog bone? Clutch type?<P>As for you comments on business I couldn't agree more.<BR>Thanks!<BR>JM||||reg||1
Z||000017||BENGAL4||07-18-2001||09:58 PM||||Slammed,<P>I have a Muncie 4 speed with 4:10 gears. It has a strut brace but it is not in the same location as the dog bone on the 2.8.<P> As for the clutch, it is a custom one they supply. They say it is better than a Centerforce. I know one thing, when Joe took me for a ride, he was going around 20mph and he stepped on it. It broke the tires. <P>This car is faster than the Mach1 Mustangs I had in my youth. Fun, fun fun.<P>Bill <BR>86GT<BR>3800 Series II S/C<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000018||fiero56||07-18-2001||10:55 PM||||You sure that car's got 4.10 gear set in it Bill? Sure didn't seem like it. I figured it was the muncie with 3.65. Not nit picking, just wondering.||||reg||1
